# .intentfiles -- WHICH DATABASE ARTEFACTS ALSO HAVE A REALISED FORM ON DISK.
#
# hv, 2026-08-19, replacing the two-region design: REALISATION IS DRIVEN FROM
# THIS FILE. Commands change it; `intent organize` realises it. Nothing
# recomputes it from status, which is why there is no protected region any
# more -- a write here is a CHANGE TO STATE, never a REGENERATION of it.
#
# Many writers, one meaning. `st new` adds the id, `st done` and `st cancel`
# remove it, `st hydrate` / `st dehydrate` do it directly, and a human may edit
# it by hand. All of those are ordinary writers;
# none is privileged.
#
# THE DATABASE ALWAYS HOLDS EVERY ARTEFACT IN FULL. This file decides only what
# is ALSO on disk, so dehydration is never a loss and hydration is a
# regeneration rather than a restore.
#
# ABSENT is not EMPTY. A missing file means nobody has said, and everything
# stays; a file present and declaring nothing means keep nothing. This file
# exists, so what it declares is the whole of what is realised.
#
# Grammar: `<SIGIL>:<ID>`, sigil STEELTHREAD -- the only one -- optional trailing
# `# comment`. Nothing else. A line the parser cannot read ABORTS the run with
# its line number -- a skipped line drops an artefact from realisation and
# leaves an estate indistinguishable from one that never listed it.
#
# It names ARTEFACTS and never FILES. `Project::classify` stays the single
# answer to what a file IS, and the two compose: STEELTHREAD:ST0056 realises
# the thread and, through classify, whatever files it produces.

# The live estate, 2026-08-19: every thread that is not completed or cancelled.
# 52 completed and 2 cancelled threads are deliberately absent -- they live in
# the store in full, and `intent st hydrate <ID>` brings any of them back.
# Issues are not named here at all: hv ruled them canon-and-store only on
# 2026-08-20 and `ISSUE:` left the grammar, so an issue has no realised form
# for this file to declare.
STEELTHREAD:ST0046
STEELTHREAD:ST0056
STEELTHREAD:ST0057
STEELTHREAD:ST0058
STEELTHREAD:ST0059
STEELTHREAD:ST0061
STEELTHREAD:ST0062
STEELTHREAD:ST0063
STEELTHREAD:ST0064
